  "intro": "This explorer documents all 31 standard Linux signals from the signal(7) man page — number, default action (terminate, core dump, ignore, stop or continue), whether the signal can be caught, and the 128+N exit code a shell reports when it kills a process. It is written for developers and SREs debugging killed processes, container shutdowns and CI failures, including PID 1 behaviour that makes docker stop hang on naive entrypoints.",
